WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Good morning, teacher and classmates. My name is Mai Như Ý, I'm in class 11A9, and this is my partner.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.800
My name is Nguyễn Thành Đạt, in class 11A9.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:15.800
Today, we are excited to present a vision of the ideal living space for humanity in the coming decades.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:28.500
That's right. Welcome to our Green City of the Future model — a place where modern technology doesn't clash with nature,
but blends with it to protect the environment and improve our quality of life. Let's explore how it works.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:39.500
Beneath the surface, the city utilizes underground water flow to run a mini hydropower station,
alongside a geothermal power plant that taps into the Earth's natural heat.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:46.200
This ensures the city is completely self-sufficient in energy with zero harmful emissions.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:58.000
Beyond clean electricity, the transportation system is also 100% eco-friendly. High above the streets,
an elevated train provides fast transit and prevents traffic jams.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.500
Down on the ground, residents use electric cars and bicycles, keeping the air fresh, clean, and quiet.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:10.800
And especially, we also feature a flying car as part of future aerial transit.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:26.000
What makes the skyscrapers here truly special is their safety and sustainability. Inside the central skyscraper,
a giant tuned mass damper (seismic pendulum) absorbs shock and keeps the building stable during strong winds or earthquakes.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:35.200
Combined with an early disaster warning radar station on the roof, extreme weather is detected early to keep residents safe.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:45.500
Surrounding the buildings are green roofs and large parks everywhere that act as the city's natural lungs.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:58.000
Through this model, we want to share a simple message: a smart city isn't just about tall buildings;
it's about respecting nature and using science for sustainable development.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:08.000
The future isn't far away — it starts with how we protect the environment today.
Thank you, teacher and everyone, for listening to our presentation!
